    "status": "FAVORABLE",
    "scope_notes": [
      "XX bonds commute mutually; bipartite coupling and exclusion of centralizer are separate claims.",
      "Generic tsum is totalized; interface for physical use requires SummableCouplingData with actual norm_summable proof."
    ]
  },
  "proved": [
    "Effective local self-adjoint bonds X_j X_(j+1) in the canonical factor.",
    "Absolute-summable coefficients produce norm-convergent potential, with uniform cutoff bound and vanishing tail.",
    "Explicit single-bond coefficients have summability proof; resulting potential is outside the centralizer when P.w 0 differs from one half.",
    "Double commutator with Z_0 and Z_1 is nonzero for every admissible profile.",
    "Certified API requires coefficient summability instead of treating a default tsum value as convergence."
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "Perturbed modular/Dyson cocycle or Duhamel estimate for its cutoff error.",
    "Identification with the modular group of a constructed perturbed state.",
    "Relativistic UV completion, quantum anomaly cancellation or RG stability in the continuum.",
    "Physical region assignment, choice of couplings, or relation of this interaction potential to reconstructed stress/metric.",
    "Mutual noncommutativity of XX bond terms; these commute."
  ],
